        <section class="guide-card" aria-labelledby="cobble-math">
          <span class="eyebrow">02 · Check the math</span>
          <h2 id="cobble-math">From stone face to order pieces</h2>
          <div class="math-grid">
            <div class="math-card">
              <h3>Paving, in square feet</h3>
              <p><code>pieces = area × 144 ÷ [(face length + joint) × (face width + joint)]</code></p>
              <p>For 100 square feet with a 9 × 5-inch face and ½-inch joint: <code>14,400 ÷ (9.5 × 5.5) = 275.6</code>. Round the layout to 276. The order is <code>ceil(275.6 × 1.08) = 298</code> with 8% extra.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="math-card">
              <h3>One border, in linear feet</h3>
              <p><code>pieces = (run × 12 + joint) ÷ (along-run face + joint)</code></p>
              <p>For 50 feet, a 9-inch along-run face, and ½-inch joints: <code>(600 + 0.5) ÷ 9.5 = 63.2</code>. Round up to 64 layout pieces; with 8% extra, order 69. The small joint adjustment treats the two open ends correctly.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>The calculator rounds the order once after applying extra to the unrounded geometric count. This avoids counting the rounding margin twice. Blocks sold in boxes or pallets may need a second round-up to the supplier's selling unit.</p>
